'''basting<sup>3</sup>''' (bās′ting), ''n.'' [Verbal n. of ''baste<sup>3</sup>''.] '''1.''' The act of sewing together with long, loose stitches.—'''2.''' The stitches themselves.

'''basting-machine''' (bās′ting-ma-shēn″), ''n.'' A sewing-machine used for basting together pieces of fabrics, to make a continuous piece for bleaching, dyeing, etc.

'''bastion''' (bas′tiọn), ''n.'' [< F. ''bastion'', < It. ''bastione'' (= Sp. ''bastion''), < ''bastire'' = OF. ''bastir'',
